    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25e8e85c_04e0a819",
        "filename": "cmd/sbox/sbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-11T21:02:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mean that sbox should treat \u0027${out}\u0027 as the first output file even when the number of output files is not equal to 1? Depending on how complex the use case is, I wonder if it would be better to have separately named output files instead",
      "parentUuid": "811bb09d_4d746f8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "1fef5212a9446275974bf900d6b83f0a45e6be72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca37fa22_d7746302",
        "filename": "cmd/sbox/sbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-19T05:40:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ick. The soong docs say that $(out) is a single output file. But without sbox, $(out) converts to Ninja\u0027s ${out}, which is a space-separate list of all output files. So we should make all of these line up. The usecases I can think of:\n\n1. Just want a list of all output files, which is what genrule does currently. In this case, just replacing __SBOX_OUT_FILE__ with a space separate list of output paths would be correct.\n2. We need to tell ninja about multiple outputs, but only pass one of them to the tool (say it takes foo.o and generates a foo.S and foo.o file). You could probably generate this path with $(genDir)/foo.o and get the right thing, but maybe we should allow some sort of labelling like $(location ...)?\n3. You give it a directory, and it writes things -- $(genDir) is enough.",
      "parentUuid": "25e8e85c_04e0a819",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "1fef5212a9446275974bf900d6b83f0a45e6be72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c5e9534_15e86677",
        "filename": "cmd/sbox/sbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-15T18:28:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does the system doing the up-to-date checks (so, Ninja) have a full list of all the expected output files in case 3 where $(out) is a directory? How does that work?\n\nIf we do want to support case #3, does that mean that if any component of $(out) is a directory, that the caller also expects sbox to copy the entire directory back to the original location? And does the caller expect sbox to wipe the destination directory first or merge them?",
      "parentUuid": "ca37fa22_d7746302",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "1fef5212a9446275974bf900d6b83f0a45e6be72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ba40194_714f3450",
        "filename": "cmd/sbox/sbox.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 91,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-15T20:31:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does the system doing the up-to-date checks (so, Ninja) have a full list of all the expected output files in case 3 where $(out) is a directory? How does that work?\n\nYeah, we still have a set of files, but we\u0027re not passing that file list to the tool, just the directory, and it (hopefully) recreates the same filenames.\n\nNinja should never be depending on the directory, since the semantics of that aren\u0027t obvious / great. So $(out) should never include a directory.",
      "parentUuid": "4c5e9534_15e86677",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "1fef5212a9446275974bf900d6b83f0a45e6be72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
