        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-16T00:27:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How would you feel (due to case 2) about making the output list be a single variable that is given following \"--outputs\u003d\" where the value is a comma separated list of output files (expressions without colons) and/or named output files (expressions with colons)? Something like this:\n\nsbox --outputs\u003dfile1:a.o,b.o,file3:subdir/c.o,otherdir/d.txt,e.dat -c \u0027myCompiler -WAll source.cc -o \"${file1}\"\u0027\n\n?\n\nThen we wouldn\u0027t expose \"$(out)\" or __SBOX_OUT_FILE__ at all since callers could give them their own names instead. We would still expose __SBOX_OUT_DIR__ though.",
      "parentUuid": "2ba40194_714f3450",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 91,
        "endChar": 80
      },
